   "speech": "From then on he lived there, showing every sign of incurable melancholia, broken from time to time by fits of the most unbridled frenzy. In his quiet spells he would play his violin for hours on end, with anguish and tears, searching for what he had lost and astonishing the doctors with the originality of certain fantasias, which he composed ceaselessly. Sometimes, amid variations on one particularly mournful theme, strange bars flew from beneath his bow that made the listeners turn pale: flashes of an exhausted beauty, hints of something greater… but this happened ever more rarely, and it ended with his death, which came in a delirium full of ardent pleas to raise the pitiless curtain that hid a mysterious and beautiful spectacle.",
